<h1><a href="#about" title="Link to section: § &#39;About&#39;">About</a></h1>
<p>Welcome to my personal website. This is a space for essays, notes, and explorations of ideas that interest me.</p>
<section id="about-me" class="level2">
<h2><a href="#about-me" title="Link to section: § &#39;About Me&#39;">About Me</a></h2>
<p>I’m a researcher and writer interested in technology, science, and the intersections between them. This website serves as my <a href="https://maggieappleton.com/garden-history" id="_AoemYD7W" class="link-live link-modified-recently" data-link-icon="maggie-appleton" data-link-icon-type="svg" data-link-icon-color="#04a4ba">digital garden</a>—a place to cultivate niggas <span class="math display">\[2x + \int 3 dx\]</span> and <span class="math inline">\(\int x dx\)</span> over time.</p>
</section>
<section id="site-philosophy" class="level2">
<h2><a href="#site-philosophy" title="Link to section: § &#39;Site Philosophy&#39;">Site Philosophy</a></h2>
<p>This site is inspired by <a href="https://gwern.net" id="_13t6WM_-" class="link-live link-modified-recently">Gwern.net</a>, one of the most thoughtfully designed personal websites on the internet. Like Gwern’s site, I aim to:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Write long-form content that improves over time</p></li>
<li><p>Use extensive annotations and citations</p></li>
<li><p>Embrace open access and transparent methodology</p></li>
<li><p>Build a interconnected web of ideas</p></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="confidence-tags" class="level2">
<h2><a href="#confidence-tags" title="Link to section: § &#39;Confidence Tags&#39;">Confidence Tags</a></h2>
<p>Pages on this site include confidence ratings to help readers calibrate:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>certain</strong>: I’m very confident this is correct</p></li>
<li><p><strong>highly-likely</strong>: Strong evidence supports this</p></li>
<li><p><strong>likely</strong>: More likely true than not</p></li>
<li><p><strong>possible</strong>: Plausible but uncertain</p></li>
<li><p><strong>unlikely</strong>: Probably not true</p></li>
<li><p><strong>log</strong>: This is a log/diary entry, not a claim</p></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="importance-tags" class="level2">
<h2><a href="#importance-tags" title="Link to section: § &#39;Importance Tags&#39;">Importance Tags</a></h2>
<p>Pages also include importance ratings from 0-10:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>10</strong>: Foundational, essential reading</p></li>
<li><p><strong>7-9</strong>: Important, worth reading carefully</p></li>
<li><p><strong>4-6</strong>: Interesting but not critical</p></li>
<li><p><strong>1-3</strong>: Minor notes or niche topics</p></li>
<li><p><strong>0</strong>: Trivial, archived for completeness</p></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="contact" class="level2">
<h2><a href="#contact" title="Link to section: § &#39;Contact&#39;">Contact</a></h2>
<p>Feel free to reach out via email or social media. I appreciate corrections, suggestions, and interesting discussions.</p>
</section>
<section id="colophon" class="level2">
<h2><a href="#colophon" title="Link to section: § &#39;Colophon&#39;">Colophon</a></h2>
<p>This site is built with:</p>
<ul>
<li><p><a href="https://jaspervdj.be/hakyll/" id="_OyLNJCN1" class="link-live link-modified-recently" data-link-icon="JVDJ" data-link-icon-type="text,quad,mono">Hakyll</a> - Static site generator in Haskell</p></li>
<li><p><a href="https://pandoc.org/" id="_0-1f5Gmb" class="link-live link-modified-recently" data-link-icon="PNDC" data-link-icon-type="text,quad,sans">Pandoc</a> - Universal document converter</p></li>
<li><p>Custom CSS and JavaScript for typography and interactivity</p></li>
</ul>
<p>The design emphasizes readability, accessibility, and information density.</p>
</section>
</section>

      
